      "compareAtPrice": 0,
      "desc": "Gotu kola over the centuries have been believed to have antimicrobial, antidiabetic, anti-inflammatory, antidepressant, and memory-enhancing properties. Some traditional uses of gotu kola by many herbalist include: Healing wounds Varicose Veins Boost Cognitive Function Relieving Diarrhea Boosting Energy Levels Reducing anxiety Enhancing Sexual Potency Treating Venereal Diseases Treating Skin Fiseases Treating Menstrual Disorders Slowing Leprosy Progression Prolonging Life Use with caution: Gotu Kola's calming effect may be amplified when taking sedatives or alcohol. Avoid taking gotu kola with Ambien (zolpidem), Ativan (lorazepam), Donnatal (phenobarbital), Klonopin (clonazepam), or other sedatives as this can lead to extreme drowsiness. **Always speak with your physician before starting an herbal regimen. These statements have not been evaluated by the Food and Drug Administration. This product is not?intended to diagnose, treat, cure, or prevent any disease. Herbalistic Wellness is a proud supporter of the National Multiple Sclerosis Society Visit them today to donate @ www.nationalmssociety.org",
      "fullDesc": "An old-soul herb for the apothecary shelf. Certified organic gotu kola (Centella asiatica) — long used in Ayurvedic tradition as a rasayana, or rejuvenative herb — is cut and sifted for your blends. It steeps into a mild, leafy, faintly sweet cup that plays well in custom tea blends alongside lemon balm, tulsi, or mint. Steep one teaspoon in just-boiled water, covered, for five to ten minutes. Store in a cool, dry place away from light. Comes in a 2 oz (56g) cut-and-sifted package.",
