      "desc": "Our line of New Herbie Ayurvedic Infusions aims to combine the ancient wisdom of herbs to educate, nature, ease, & support promoting balance between the mind, body and spirit elements.\n\n?These unique tea blends are meant to re align imbalances & bring you back into a healthy vibration within the world around us.?\n\nAyurveda teaches us that there are three types of sleep deficiencies. Each relates to one of the three doshas, or what we consider our mind-body types: Vata, Kapha and Pitta.\n\n-Vata dosha relates most directly to one's mental state, a Vata sleep disorder commonly presents itself in a restless mind, creating an inability to fall into a deep sleep, which can be counteracted with soothing lavender.\n\n-Kapha dosha typically effect one's ability to recover from sleep; often times leaving one feeling lethargic and groggy after a full night's rest, which is best counteracted with chamomile.\n\n?-Pitta dosha are more emotional in nature, but tend to present themselves biologically while interrupting sleep with symptoms that may include hot flashes, which can be avoided with the use of cooling gotu kola.\n\nSo make sure to do your own research on Ayurveda.?\n\nThis unique blend contains Organic chamomile flower, organic gotu kola leaf, organic orange peel, organic lavender flower, organic cinnamon bark, organic valerian root powder, organic licorice root and organic cardamom seed.\n\nPerfect for the Herbie looking for a natural alternative.?\n\n\n\n\nThese statements have not been evaluated by the FDA. This product is not intended to diagnose, treat, cure or prevent any disease. Consult your physician before taking any dietary supplements if you are pregnant or nursing, if you have a medical condition, or are taking medication. Keep out of reach of children",
      "fullDesc": "Our master Ayurvedic bedtime blend. Organic ashwagandha root, whole chamomile flowers, valerian root, lavender buds, and ground nutmeg — the classic herbs of the nighttime cup, long treasured in Ayurvedic tradition. It brews a warm, honeyed, faintly sweet cup with a soft floral finish. About an hour before bed, brew a strong cup, dim the lights, and let the steaming ritual tell your body the day is done. Steep one tablespoon in just-boiled water, covered, for ten to fifteen minutes. Caffeine-free. Store in a cool, dry place away from light.",
