      "desc": "A Herbalistic Wellness Lavender Oatmeal & Honey milk bath leaves your skin feeling soft and supple. The fat and protein in the milk provide this immediate benefit in your bathwater. The milk also helps exfoliate the skin for additional softness. The lactic acid in milk helps clean, soften, and removes dead skin cells helping the milk to hydrates the skin, preventing dryness.\n\n\nMany adults and children experience uncomfortable skin irritations such as eczema. A milk bath may help soothe some of the irritation of eczema and other skin conditions. Make sure to check with your health-care provider before trying home remedies for a medical skin condition.\n\n\nThe soothing feeling of the milk in the water combined with the essential oils of lavender & vanilla, collidial oatmeal, and the honey powder creates an overall relaxed, comfortable feeling. Taking a milk bath at the end of the day can help you improve your skin while the lavender helps to reduce the stress of your day. Try to create an overall relaxing environment by dimming the lights, using candles and playing relaxing music in the background, turn your bath time into your personal spa today.\n\n\nThese statements have not been evaluated by the Food and Drug Administration. This product is not?intended to diagnose, treat, cure, or prevent any disease.\n\n\nHerbalistic Wellness is a proud supporter of the National Multiple Sclerosis Society Visit them today to donate @ www.nationalmssociety.org",
      "fullDesc": "The Cleopatra treatment, minus the palace. Organic coconut milk powder, micronized colloidal oatmeal, pure honey powder, Epsom salts, and French lavender oil swirl into bathwater and turn it silky, milky, and fragrant. Pour a generous scoop under warm running water, sink in, and stay a while — this is the long-soak, candles-lit, phone-in-another-room kind of bath. Rinse lightly after, pat dry, and follow with your favorite body oil. For external use only. If your skin is easily irritated, patch-test first.",
