      "compareAtPrice": 0,
      "desc": "Marshmallow root also known as (Althaea officinalis) has a very long history in ancient medicine, a plant native to Africa and many other countries even going back to ancient Greek and Egyptian times.\n\nOver 2,800 years ago, references to this plant were a popular way to ease coughs, sore throats and congestion. Some herbalist make herbal cough syrups and cough drops containing marshmallow root, Improving dry mouth.\n\nProtects against ulcers, helping to repair the gut lining, The roots and stem of the marshmallow plant secrete mucilage, which softens skin, lowers swelling and kills bacteria.\n\nAlso known to soothes skin irritation promoting wound regeneration, ease and supporting the throat from gastric reflux.",
      "fullDesc": "The apothecary's gentle giant. Organic marshmallow root is a classic demulcent herb — steeped long in cold water it gives a smooth, silky, softly sweet infusion with a naturally soothing mouthfeel. Folk herbalists have reached for it for generations, and it blends beautifully with mint, chamomile, or licorice root. For the silkiest cup, do a cold-water infusion: stir one tablespoon into a quart of cool water, cover, and rest in the fridge overnight, then strain. Store in a cool, dry place away from light.",
