      "cat": "specialty-blends",
      "price": 15,
      "compareAtPrice": 0,
      "desc": "Is it good to use shea butter as a daily moisturizer for your skin?\n\nDid you know that the high concentrations of fatty acids and vitamins make shea butter an ideal cosmetic ingredient?for softening and repairing skin.\n\nShea butter is a fat extracted from the nut of the African shea tree. It is ivory in color when raw and commonly dyed yellow with borututu root or palm oil.\n\nShea butter is known for it's anti-inflammatory and healing properties. Using shea butter on your body, especially your face, can condition, tone, and soothe your skin\n\nShea butter takes four days to clear nasal congestion, three months to soothe and soften skin, and up to six months to eliminate or reduce scars. You should leave shea butter applied for eight hours daily.\n\nShea butter is long lasting natural moisturizer but can go bad after about 12 months, so ensure you use it enough to keep it from going rancid.\n\nUsed topically, Shea Butter is known to be a ?skin superfood? that nourishes skin to promote its clarity and addresses problems such as dryness, blemishes, dark spots, discolorations, stretch marks, and wrinkles without clogging pores. It's even a great product to use in natural hair. With this fragrance free all natural vegan moisturizer packaged in Herbalistic Wellness signature glass reusable containers you can not go wrong with this purchase!!\n\n\n\n\nThese statements have not been evaluated by the Food and Drug Administration. This product is not?intended to diagnose, treat, cure, or prevent any disease.\n\n\nHerbalistic Wellness is a proud supporter of the National Multiple Sclerosis Society Visit them today to donate @ www.nationalmssociety.org",
      "fullDesc": "The one-jar wonder. Ethically sourced Grade A unrefined Ghanaian shea butter, whipped into a luxurious velvet cloud with golden jojoba. Rich in vitamins A, E, and F, this fragrance-free all-purpose butter seals in moisture — scoop a little and work it into dry hands, elbows, knees, and heels, or smooth it through the ends of your hair. A little goes a long way; warm it between your palms first and it melts like, well, butter. For external use only.",
