      "compareAtPrice": 0,
      "desc": "Nature?s ultimate seasonal defender, concentrated for daily resilience.\nWhen your system needs an extra layer of protection against environmental stressors, look no further than the deep purple power of the European Black Elderberry (Sambucus nigra). Our Elderberry Tincture delivers the concentrated wellness of this time-tested botanical in a travel-friendly, fast-acting liquid format.\n\nElderberries are celebrated for their exceptionally high concentration of anthocyanins and vitamin C, making them an absolute powerhouse for neutralizing free radicals and reinforcing cellular health. Instead of sugary syrups, our clean tincture format offers a pure, potent extract that assimilates quickly into your system. It is the perfect daily ritual to keep your immune defenses robust and your body thriving through every changing season.\n\nKey Benefits\nYear-Round Immune Backing: Provides targeted nourishment to support and strengthen your body?s natural immune response.\nAntioxidant Powerhouse: Packed with dark berry flavonoids that combat everyday oxidative stress and support cellular longevity.\nUpper Respiratory Support: Helps maintain healthy respiratory function, keeping you feeling clear and vibrant during seasonal transitions.\nPure & Sugar-Free: All the defensive benefits of fresh elderberries without the added sugars, artificial thickeners, or preservatives found in commercial syrups.\n\nPure Ingredients\nOrganic Black Elderberry (Sambucus nigra) fruit\nOrganic Cane Alcohol (extraction agent)\n\nSuggested Use\nFor Daily Maintenance: Take 1 dropperful (approx. 30 drops) in water or juice, 1 to 2 times daily.\nFor Extra Seasonal Support: Take 1 to 2 dropperfuls up to 4 times daily, or as recommended by your holistic health professional.\nShake well before use. Store in a cool, dark place.\n\nRegulatory Note: These statements have not been evaluated by the Food and Drug Administration. This product is not intended to diagnose, treat, cure, or prevent any disease. Consult your healthcare provider before use if you are pregnant, nursing, or taking regular medications.",
